{"id":108566848949068,"type":"song","name":"Still Loving You","artist":"The Scorpions","year":1984,"weight":10,"info":{"img":null},"artist_ref":{"id":207671290867672,"name":"The Scorpions","info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Scorpions_in_Kavarna_2010.JPG?width=500"}},"labels":[],"genres":[],"lists":[],"podcast":[{"kind":"podcast","title":null,"body":"This song is cited as a prime example of a ballad found on metal albums, illustrating the \"twin musical threads of sonic aggression and acoustic intimacy\" within the genre. Such ballads were strategically used to slow the pace, engage the audience, and by contrast, intensify the impact of the louder sections. \"It's not just the ballads that always seem to be part of the metal albums. You know, like still loving you by the scorpions or something like that.\"","year":1984,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"For the Record - The 70s","episode":"Ep. 24 - Loud, Louder, Loudest - 70s Heavy Metal","url":"https://seventies.libsyn.com/ep-24-loud-louder-loudest-70s-heavy-metal"},{"source":"For the Record - The 70s","episode":"Ep. 24 - Loud, Louder, Loudest - 70s Heavy Metal","url":null}]}],"book_tracks":[],"others":[{"id":141560515385417,"type":"song","name":"Rock You Like a Hurricane","year":1984,"weight":19},{"id":1202921131968,"type":"song","name":"Wind of Change","year":1991,"weight":17},{"id":251372856843827,"type":"album","name":"Love at First Sting","year":1984,"weight":11},{"id":234543095830095,"type":"work","name":"He’s a Woman – She’s a Man","year":1977,"weight":6},{"id":231901207598585,"type":"work","name":"World Wide Live","year":1985,"weight":6},{"id":193589989728078,"type":"work","name":"Backstage Queen","year":1974,"weight":6},{"id":97118361366009,"type":"work","name":"Bad Boys Running Wild","year":1984,"weight":6},{"id":82404599033740,"type":"work","name":"Animal Magnetism","year":1980,"weight":6},{"id":26300602021340,"type":"work","name":"Twentieth Century Man","year":1980,"weight":6